      "independent_visual": {
        "assessment": {
          "concrete_defects": [
            "Closed viewer lid reads pale lavender/gray and streaky rather than clearly indigo with ivory resist loops; its ornament/pattern contrast is notably weaker than the patterned body and the promotional lid.",
            "Small raised rosettes lose openwork/petal legibility in the mobile closed view; the defining craft detail becomes small yellow-gold marks.",
            "Viewer body shows horizontal tonal banding, while panel borders create conspicuous abrupt pattern breaks; registration resets are intentional but remain visually prominent.",
            "Mobile lid/rim/fittings have jagged edges and rough gray feet lose detail against the dark base."
          ],
          "id": "indonesia",
          "inspected_paths": [
            "parent/smoke/indonesia/desktop-closed.png",
            "parent/smoke/indonesia/desktop-open.png",
            "parent/smoke/indonesia/mobile-closed.png",
            "parent/smoke/indonesia/mobile-open.png",
            "parent/sources/indonesia/marketing.webp"
          ],
          "limitations": [
            "All five original images inspected individually with vision; paths relative to launch/qa-art-08. Source readme and research brief also consulted for intended design.",
            "Static views cannot prove hidden attachment, contact, collision clearance or motion; unseen faces are unassessed.",
            "Promotional artwork is not an exact model reference or evidence of mechanics; differences are presentation observations, not geometry parity failures.",
            "Inherited visual hold remains. This review neither changes artwork nor grants approval.",
            "Panel pattern resets, dark stone feet, brass family hardware and a pronounced seam are documented design choices; terrain is not required for this craft-themed design."
          ],
          "observations": [
            "Independent reason to preserve hold: the headline indigo/ivory and copper-openwork identity is unevenly communicated by the actual closed lid, especially at mobile scale. User review is warranted despite intact page framing.",
            "All four viewer states fit without obvious cropping or controls overlap; open patterned interior and lid are readable.",
            "Gold/brass-looking fittings alone are not a material defect because family brass hardware is explicitly retained. The exposed upper tab and pronounced seam are visually ambiguous, not proof of mechanical failure.",
            "Promotion is fully framed and more clearly communicates the repeated loop motif, but has an uneven dark lid seam and irregular ornament contours. Its polish cannot clear the actual viewer hold."
          ],
          "verdict": "needs-user-review"
        },
        "report": "visual-b.json"
      },
